name c01m02-night-forger
timeout 300
time 1994-10-07T06:00:00Z

# ARMORED FIST (NovaLogic 1994), CAMPAIGN ONE "OVERWATCH", MISSION 2 OF 7 — `INDIA2`, NIGHT FORGER.
# THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES D1-D7 are stated in full in c01m01-slaughterzone.fbm and apply here unchanged:
# no tracked vehicle exists so Echo flies as `f16`, one jet per [GUIDE] vehicle (D1); red has no weapon
# and no sensor, so this mission is not losable (D2); one pass per unit (D3); two fragility classes,
# `target_hard` = T-80, `target_soft` = BMP-2 (D4); real Sindh/Rajasthan DEM (D5); the layout inside the
# box is [SET] (D6); the clock is the CD's file date at 1100 PKT (D7).
#
# THE TASK [FSW]: break free of the enemy's fields of fire and NEUTRALISE ALL FIELDED INDIAN MBTs AND
# IFVs. Time limit 5 MIN — the shortest in the campaign [FSG, SHDR byte 5], and the mission-defining
# number.
#
# TWO CONTRADICTIONS THIS FILE CARRIES RATHER THAN RESOLVES (campaign.md §4):
#   (a) THE NAME. `INDIA2.FSW`'s header reads `NIGHT FORGER.` and the guide's chapter agrees, but the
#       campaign-map screenshot printed as Figure 4-1 on [GUIDE p.53] labels the same mission
#       `Reforger` — both legible, both from the same book. The file name follows the briefing, which
#       is the game's own text.
#   (b) THE LIGHT. [GUIDE p.58] calls this "your first night mission … working with the thermal
#       sights". The DATA says otherwise: `INDIA2` loads `2.SKY` with palette `232`, the daylight pair
#       the mission editor names WINDY MEADOWS, while the one nocturnal asset (`7.SKY`, one fifth the
#       size of every other sky and absent from the editor table) is loaded by `INDIA5` alone [FSG].
#       THE MEASUREMENT BEATS THE PROSE: this file is flown in daylight (0600Z = 1100 PKT, measured sun
#       elevation 54 deg) and mission 5 is the campaign's only night mission. Most likely the guide was
#       written against a pre-release build; that is a guess and is not asserted.
#
# NO COURSE IS STATED [FSW] — this is a running fight, not an advance. The axis used here is the
# MEASURED one: `PATH` slot 0's net bearing over its nine waypoints, 250.3 deg, under the +X-east /
# +Y-north convention established at 35.9 deg mean error over twelve briefed headings (campaign.md
# §7.2). It is the only mission in Overwatch whose axis comes from the file rather than from prose.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DECLARES
#   Blue [GUIDE p.58]: Echo 1 = 1 M1A2 + 1 M3. Two vehicles, two jets, two passes, three enemy platoons.
#   Red  [GUIDE p.58]: Bandit 1 (2 T-80, 2 BMP), Bandit 2 (3 T-80, 1 BMP), Bandit 3 (2 T-80, 2 BMP).
#   All twelve are goals, because the [FSW] task says ALL fielded MBTs and IFVs.
#
# WHAT THE 5-MINUTE LIMIT DOES HERE AND WHY IT IS NOT THE ORIGINAL'S CONSTRAINT. 300 s at 231 m/s is
# 69 km; the run-in is 40 km and the release falls near t = 165 s. A jet therefore beats a limit that
# was set for tracked vehicles, and the reading rule's "a run that stops to fight in place is a fail"
# has no object: nothing here can stop, and nothing here can be fought. The limit is kept because it is
# the one hard measured number the mission file carries; its bite is gone, and that is the substitution
# talking, not the engine.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `m2e1a`'s UNIT_RESULT and nothing else.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires all twelve red vehicles dead inside 300 s. TIMEOUT/exit 3 with a subset
#   dead is EXPECTED: two passes, three platoons, and seven of the twelve are T-80s no weapon in this
#   tree reaches (D3, D4). Count DESTROYED against INTACT and report the split.
#   exit 1 on a blue unit is an ENGINE finding, not a mission loss (D2).

unit m2e1a
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight echo1 1
  spawn 26.71550 71.18092 1150 250.3 450      # 40 km up-track of Bandit 1 on the MEASURED axis 250.3
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 cbu87
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 26.57844 70.79246 1150 450               # AIM POINT: Bandit 1
  wp 26.51806 70.56615 1750 450               # egress 25 km down the axis
  objective kill unit m2b1v1
  objective kill unit m2b1v2
  objective kill unit m2b1v3
  objective kill unit m2b1v4
  objective kill unit m2b2v1
  objective kill unit m2b2v2
  objective kill unit m2b2v3
  objective kill unit m2b2v4
  objective kill unit m2b3v1
  objective kill unit m2b3v2
  objective kill unit m2b3v3
  objective kill unit m2b3v4
  objective survive

unit m2e1b
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight echo1 2
  spawn 26.72822 71.17583 1150 250.3 450      # 1.5 km across track
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 cbu87
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 26.58793 70.78368 1150 450               # AIM POINT: Bandit 2, the strongest platoon (3 T-80)
  wp 26.51806 70.56615 1750 450
  objective survive

# ---- BANDIT 1 [GUIDE p.58]: 2 T-80, 2 BMP
unit m2b1v1
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.57793 70.79267 ground 250.3 0
unit m2b1v2
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.57827 70.79253 ground 250.3 0
unit m2b1v3
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.57861 70.79240 ground 250.3 0
unit m2b1v4
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.57895 70.79226 ground 250.3 0

# ---- BANDIT 2 [GUIDE p.58]: 3 T-80, 1 BMP
unit m2b2v1
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.58742 70.78389 ground 250.3 0
unit m2b2v2
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.58776 70.78375 ground 250.3 0
unit m2b2v3
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.58809 70.78362 ground 250.3 0
unit m2b2v4
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.58843 70.78348 ground 250.3 0

# ---- BANDIT 3 [GUIDE p.58]: 2 T-80, 2 BMP. No delivery unit left for it (D3).
unit m2b3v1
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.59974 70.78396 ground 250.3 0
unit m2b3v2
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.60008 70.78382 ground 250.3 0
unit m2b3v3
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.60042 70.78369 ground 250.3 0
unit m2b3v4
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.60076 70.78355 ground 250.3 0
